  <section>
    <h2>Release, source, and licenses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/getrelaybridge/relaybridge/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.1">RelayBridge v1.0.0-rc.1 GitHub Release</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/getrelaybridge/relaybridge/tree/v1.0.0-rc.1">Exact v1.0.0-rc.1 tagged source</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/getrelaybridge/relaybridge">RelayBridge application repository</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/getrelaybridge/website">RelayBridge website repository</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>RelayBridge-owned application source is MPL-2.0. The separate website repository is MIT-licensed. Microsoft, WiX, .NET, PowerShell, ExchangeOnlineManagement, Graph, Entra, and other third-party components retain their respective licenses.</p>
    <p>Installed reference documents are available under <code>C:\Program Files\RelayBridge\Docs</code> as <code>GETTING-STARTED.md</code>, <code>LICENSE</code>, and <code>THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Support, security, and contributions</h2>
    <p>Use <a href="https://github.com/getrelaybridge/relaybridge/issues">GitHub Issues</a> for reproducible non-security bugs and feature discussions. Report suspected vulnerabilities privately as directed by <a href="https://github.com/getrelaybridge/relaybridge/blob/main/SECURITY.md">SECURITY.md</a>.</p>
    <p>Do not publish tenant identifiers, mailbox or message data, credentials, tokens, certificates, private keys, raw configuration, databases, spool files, or unreviewed support bundles.</p>
    <p>Public application contributions use a focused branch, tests, a DCO <code>Signed-off-by</code> trailer, CI, and a pull request. RelayBridge uses DCO 1.1 and does not require a CLA.</p>
    <div class="docs-related">
      <a href="/docs/operations/diagnostics/"><strong>Diagnostics and support bundles</strong><span>Collect and review the implemented bounded evidence export.</span></a>
      <a href="/docs/security/"><strong>Security and limitations</strong><span>Review the residual risks and current RC1 product boundaries.</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
